{"kind":"artifact","text":"host at exact clean pushed head 2df37050b990d59013ba9d119d3faae0c966148e on request/config-cross-process-cas, answering 9da2d677 under my promise 91c51d48.\n\nInit wrote its first configuration through SaveConfig, which overwrites. Codex named this path in finding two of ec70f908: with generic mutation no longer creating a missing file, the initialization contract has to be explicit, and an overwriting write at init means a lost double-init race is silent. It now uses CreateConfig, whose exclusive creation makes that race loud instead.\n\nNothing else in this package changes, and no behaviour changes for a first init that wins its race.\n\nOne gap I am reporting rather than leaving for a reviewer to find: no test pins this call site to exclusive creation. Reverting it to SaveConfig runs green. The window between the absence check and the write has no injection seam, and adding a production gate solely to test it seemed worse than the gap. CreateConfigs own exclusivity is covered by its existing suite; what is unpinned is only that this site keeps using it.","body":{"commit":"2df37050b990d59013ba9d119d3faae0c966148e","path":"host"}}